Fix an ``IndexError`` crash when inferring an argument of a function whose
keyword-only parameter shares the name of the ``*args`` parameter (e.g.
``def f(x, *y, y): ...``). The shared name dropped the keyword-only entry from
the positional list, so ``Arguments.default_value`` computed an index past the
end of ``defaults``; it now reports no default in that case, matching what the
caller already expects.

Closes #3259
